# Change Discipline

## Purpose

Protect legacy surfaces and keep diffs reviewable by implementing only what was asked.

## When Applied

Always, on every edit and PR.

## Requirements

- Implement only the requested change; no opportunistic cleanups.
- Prefer **additive consistency** (new code follows conventions) over broad renames.
- Keep admin god-repositories (`CoachRepository`, `AdminRepository`, etc.) incremental — extract only when asked.
- Docs/rules-only tasks must not touch Flutter source under `lib/`.
- Call out, don't silently perform, any change that grows in scope.

## Examples

- Asked to add a field → touch the one model + repo + widget path, nothing else.
- Spot an unrelated typo → leave it, or note it separately.

## Anti-patterns

- Deleting `lib/view/`, the unused `provider` dependency, or `navigation_bloc` without an explicit request.
- Reformatting or renaming files unrelated to the task.

## Common Mistakes

- "While I was here I also refactored X" — this breaks review and blame.
- Fixing typos in unrelated files while delivering a feature.
